From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] PS4: the 32-bit GPU window in RADV's cache UUID (a pipeline cache
 built for another window is ignored)

Compiled shaders hold address32_hi, and on the PS4 the 32-bit window is wherever the kernel
reserved it that session. Eden for PS4 03.84 had it at 0x9600000000; the pipelines built then
stayed in the app's pipeline cache file and loaded in later versions (window 0x4400000000),
reading their descriptors from unmapped memory: Captain Toad Treasure Tracker's level 3 faulted
the GPU on them.

---
 src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/radv_physical_device.c
@@ -334,6 +334,16 @@
       return -1;
 #endif
 
+   /* PS4: compiled shaders hold the upper half of the 32-bit GPU address window (address32_hi:
+    * "s_movk_i32 s3, 0x44" before each descriptor set load), and on the PS4 that window is wherever
+    * the kernel reserved it that session (port/mesa/ac_ps4_drm.c). Eden for PS4 03.84 had it at
+    * 0x9600000000: the pipelines built then went into the app's pipeline cache file and kept
+    * loading in later versions (window at 0x4400000000), reading their descriptors from memory the
+    * GPU no longer maps - a GPU fault (Captain Toad Treasure Tracker's level 3, Eden 04.57). The
+    * window in the UUID: the pipeline cache header and the disk cache keys change with it, and a
+    * cache built for another window is ignored and rebuilt. (On Linux address32_hi is fixed.) */
+   _mesa_sha1_update(&ctx, &pdev->info.address32_hi, sizeof(pdev->info.address32_hi));
+
    _mesa_sha1_final(&ctx, sha1);
 
    memcpy(uuid, sha1, VK_UUID_SIZE);
